# Build-time defaults for production builds of the web app (Vite inlines VITE_* at build time).
#
# Why this file is committed: without these values the bundle throws on load and the deployed site is a blank page.
# Everything here is PUBLIC by design — the Supabase URL and the publishable ("anon") key ship inside every browser
# bundle, and they grant nothing on their own: the anon role holds zero table privileges and row-level security denies
# it every row (see supabase/migrations/…_rls_policies.sql and docs/security.md).
#
# NEVER put a service-role key, a database password, FLOWZA_CREDENTIALS_MASTER_KEYS or any provider credential here.
# Those are server-side secrets and belong in the platform's secret store.
#
# Overriding per environment: a real environment variable set by the host or CI takes precedence over this file, so a
# staging deployment that sets VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY uses its own project. The flip side is that an
# environment which sets nothing silently falls back to the project below — so set them explicitly for any deployment
# that is not this one.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://liyilmbklsextsggflbb.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_SDK8x_KVhjgXxrk-xvJ0Xw__LWSJIQF

# The API origin, matching fly.api.toml's API_PUBLIC_URL. That deployment's WEB_ORIGINS must in turn list this site's
# origin (https://time.flowza.ai) or the browser rejects every response as a CORS failure.
#
# Leaving this unset is not neutral: src/lib/env.ts falls back to http://localhost:4000, so a deployed bundle asks the
# visitor's own machine for data. Sign-in still works (that goes straight to Supabase Auth), so the app looks healthy
# right up to the first request, then every one of them fails with ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED — a missing setting wearing
# the costume of a broken backend.
VITE_API_URL=https://time-api.flowza.ai
